## Preparation notes (supplied)
N01. Chosen as the first v2 package because the layout itself is the newest uncertain design piece.
N02. The whole contract file is the target; it is short and its sections depend on each other.
N03. Hostile-read mode: the most useful result is a concrete confusion path, not agreement.

## Supplied purpose
Where could the four-file exchange let a template, a note or a placed return be mistaken for a completed review, an edited return or a release?

The exchange is meant to keep exact return custody and Prime's assessment apart. If a reader can confuse them, a Colab's words could be silently promoted, or a review could appear complete when no review happened.

## Supplied context
The Director agreed an exchange for actual N7NN investigations: a pack and a return share 05.NN, and notes and a review share 06.NN. The target contract is Prime's bounded interpretation of that agreement. A producer (0510/05.03) prepares the pack, notes and templates. Workflow placement of the return and the review is not built yet.

## Supplied known gaps
G01. No investigation member exists in 0700.band.colabs yet; this binding names a declared fixture page.
G02. Workflow naming integration is pending and is not part of this package.

